@startuml
!include theme.puml
title ERP | Actors and core use cases
left to right direction
actor Student as S
actor "Staff\n(instructor / employee)" as T
actor Admin as A
actor "Super admin" as SA
actor "Payment provider" as P
rectangle "ERP: web screens + business APIs" {
  usecase "Authenticate /\nrotate session" as login
  usecase "Enroll + view\nasynchronous invoice" as enroll
  usecase "Register offering /\ncheck prerequisites" as register
  usecase "View grades /\nappeal / PDF reports" as grades
  usecase "Pay tuition /\ndownload receipt" as pay
  usecase "Manage teaching,\nexams and appeals\n(API-only staff UI gap)" as teaching
  usecase "Fees / expenses /\ncampaigns / summaries\n(API-only staff UI gap)" as finance
  usecase "Own leave, check-in,\nnotifications, payslips" as own
  usecase "Recruitment / assets /\nleave decisions / payroll\n(API-only admin UI gap)" as hr
  usecase "Attest payroll\nrate schedule" as attest
  usecase "Obtain provider\nsettlement status" as status
}
S --> login
T --> login
A --> login
SA --> login
S --> enroll
S --> register
S --> grades
S --> pay
T --> teaching
T --> finance
T --> own
A --> teaching
A --> finance
A --> hr
SA --> hr
SA --> attest
pay ..> status : <<include>>
P --> status
note bottom of teaching
Staff teaching actions require assigned offering.
Admin and super-admin may manage offerings.
UI route guard authenticates; page-level checks
show student/staff content or explicit placeholders.
end note
note bottom of attest
Attestation is manual, not automated tax validation.
Tenant context is required for ordinary mutations.
Actors describe permissions, not implemented admin screens.
end note
@enduml
